# Accepted risks for the whole project. Resource-specific exceptions sit next to
# the resource as #trivy:ignore comments.

# Customer-managed encryption keys (Cloud KMS). GCP already encrypts every disk
# and bucket at rest with Google-managed keys. CMEK is for compliance that asks
# for own keys; in this lab it only adds cost, and a KMS key ring can never be
# deleted, so destroy followed by apply would fail on the existing name.
GCP-0033
GCP-0034
